[Unit]
Description=GPU woken from deep idle at each key or pointer event - Intel Xe out of gt-c6 (also kept up while it draws under CPU load, and poked when its temperature reading is stale), AMD with GFXOFF held off for 0.3 s: ~1.2-2 ms less key latency on the Arc Pro B50, ~0.5-0.8 ms (p90 ~1.3) on the RX 6900 XT, nothing at rest
Documentation=file:///usr/local/sbin/gpu-input-awake
After=sys-kernel-debug.mount systemd-udevd.service
Wants=sys-kernel-debug.mount
# with an Intel Xe/i915 GPU or an AMD one: the script waits up to 60 s for the driver's debugfs forcewake_all or
# amdgpu_gfxoff and exits quietly without either (since 2026-10-28 AMD has a backend; --activity and --temp-refresh
# are the Xe's and switch themselves off there). Not a ConditionPathExistsGlob (until 2026-10-23): checked once at
# start, it raced xe's probe - xe registers its debugfs ~150-200 ms after its "Initialized" line - and two of three
# boots skipped the service

[Service]
# --hold 0.02 (2026-10-22, b50wh2/b50whk): the whole gain down to 0.01 s (keys 9.0 -> 7.6 ms, typing into Konsole
# 22.7 -> 21.1 ms) for +1.4-2.1 W while typing non-stop, against +8.4 W with the first --hold 3
# --activity (2026-10-22 night, b50act): also while the GT draws continuously and the CPUs are busy - a 60 fps video under a
# compile 54.8-85.3 % -> 97.7-98.5 % on cadence (display-resample); idle and a compile without drawing: no hold, 21.7 W
# --vm-activity (2026-10-22 night, b50vmvid / b50vmvidfw): a running VM counts as load - a 60 fps video in the nested VM on an
# idle host 27.6-47.5 % on cadence (display-resample) with the GT free to idle, 100 % held
# --activity-hold 10 --sample 0.05 (b50vmvidva): the hold lapses to look again only every 10 s, for 50 ms - the VM video's
# few late frames (97.2-99.2 % with 4 s / 0.1 s) fell in those windows
# --temp-refresh 2 (2026-10-23, b50fr / b50fs): the card's "pkg" temperature freezes while the GT sleeps and the fan follows it -
# after a load the blower held ~3,000 rpm for minutes; a 20 ms GT wake every 2 s while the fan spins above 1,500 rpm (or "pkg"
# reads 2 C above the memory controller) lets the fan glide down with the card (< 1,500 rpm in ~50 s), nothing at rest
# --busy-samples 2 (the default since 2026-10-24, b50vi1-3): a hold needs two consecutive drawing samples - with one, a
# stray idle job of the VM held the GT for 10 s at a time (the idle VM 25.7 W, C6 68 % instead of 22.1 W, 100 %); a
# 60 fps video in the VM still holds it (display-resample 98.2-99.4 %, b50vv3)
# --vm-hold S (2026-11-07, not set): the hold while a VM runs - on the B50 0.3 s kept the GT awake for every key while
# typing in a VM (keys ~0.5 ms sooner in every VM path, ~+5 W while typing, nothing at rest; the 20 ms hold let it sleep
# before every key), the bare desktop keeping its 20 ms (findings/b50-day-2026-11-06.md X6d, X6i, X6j). An improvement,
# not the default for now (the user, 11-07: 0.5 ms is not something they would notice); to try it, add --vm-hold 0.3
ExecStart=/usr/bin/python3 -B /usr/local/sbin/gpu-input-awake --hold 0.02 --activity --vm-activity --activity-hold 10 --sample 0.05 --temp-refresh 2
Restart=on-failure
RestartSec=5

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
